hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"17357","Haddathana Hajjaj, he said akhbarana Layth ibn Sad, he said haddathani Uqayl, from Ibn Shihab, from Ibn Abi Namlah, that Abu Namlah al-Ansari informed him that while he was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came to him and said: O Muhammad, does this bier speak. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Allah knows best. The Jew said: I testify that it speaks. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: When the People of the Book narrate to you, do not believe them nor belie them, and say: We believe in Allah and His books and His messengers, for if it is truth you have not belied them, and if it is falsehood you have not believed them."
"17358","Haddathana Uthman ibn Umar, he said haddathana Yunus, from al-Zuhri, he said akhbarani Ibn Abi Namlah, that his father narrated to him, he said: While I was sitting with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), a man from the Jews came to him, then he mentioned the like of it, except he said: and His book and His messengers."
